                "literalString": "1. Grounding skills for flashbacks"
              },
              "variant": "bodySemibold",
              "color": "label"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "grounding_md",
          "component": {
            "MarkdownView": {
              "text": {
                "literalString": "**How it helps:** Grounding brings your attention back to the present when your brain is reacting as if the danger is happening again.\n\n**Why it matters:** In a flashback, your body can go into survival mode—heart racing, scanning for threat, feeling like you are back there. Grounding helps remind your senses: *I am here, now; the memory is real, but the danger is not happening in this moment.*\n\n**Examples:**\n- Name **5 things you see**, **4 you feel**, **3 you hear**\n- Press your boots or feet into the floor\n- Hold something cold\n- Look around and say the date, place, and who is with you\n- Slow your exhale longer than your inhale"
              }
            }
          }
        },
