              "text": {
                "literalString": "**How it helps:** A trauma-informed therapist can help you process the war memories instead of getting ambushed by them.\n\n**Why it matters:** Trauma can leave memories stored in a raw, alarm-heavy way. Treatment can help reduce the intensity of triggers, nightmares, guilt, anger, and avoidance.\n\n**What it can look like:**\n- Talking through patterns and triggers\n- Learning tools for sleep, panic, and anger\n- Structured PTSD treatments through veteran or community services\n- Building a plan for what to do when memories of Iraq hit hard"
